.TH LIGINT 1 "" "ligint @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ligint \- non-covalent ligand-protein interactions from a PDB or mmCIF file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ligint
.I structure
.RI [ RESNAME
.RI [ chain
.RI [ resseq\c
.RB [ A | \- ]]]]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ligint
finds the non-covalent interactions between a ligand (a HETATM residue) and the protein of a PDB or PDBx/mmCIF file:
hydrogen bonds, salt bridges, hydrophobic contacts, pi-stacking, cation-pi, halogen bonds, metal coordination
and water bridges, plus steric clashes and electrostatic repulsions.
It can also summarize them as an interaction fingerprint (one row per protein residue, one column per
interaction class) in CSV, JSON or SVG.
.PP
With only
.I structure
it lists the ligands present (and the alternate conformations of the file, if any).
With
.I RESNAME
it analyzes every copy of that ligand; a chain and a residue number select a single copy.
The residue number accepts an insertion code:
.B 501
(any code),
.B 501A
(code A) or
.B 501\-
(no code).
.PP
The chemistry of the ligand (donors, acceptors, charges) is inferred from the geometry unless an SDF or MOL2
template is given. See the documentation for the assumptions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Write the interactions as CSV on standard output (service information goes to standard error).
.TP
.BI \-\-sdf " FILE" ", " \-\-mol2 " FILE"
Chemical annotation of the ligand (bond orders, explicit hydrogens, formal charges). The ligand of the PDB file is
matched to the molecule by coordinates.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-water
Ignore water molecules (no water bridges).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-merge
Do not merge covalently linked HETATM residues (glycans, dipeptides) into a single ligand.
.TP
.B \-\-plip\-like
Preset for the comparison with PLIP:
.BR "\-\-hb\-long 4.1 \-\-salt\-centroid 5.5 \-\-hal\-max 4.0" .
Explicit options take precedence.
.TP
.B \-\-metal\-donors
Let O and N coordinated to a metal remain possible hydrogen-bond donors.
.TP
.B \-\-backbone\-hyd
Count apolar contacts with the protein backbone.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Format of the structure file:
.BR auto
(default, recognized from the content),
.B pdb
or
.BR cif .
Compressed (gzip) files must be decompressed first.
.TP
.BI \-\-altloc " X"
Use the alternate conformation
.I X
for the residues that have it; the others keep their first conformation.
.TP
.BI \-\-fingerprint " FORMAT"
Write the interaction fingerprint instead of the interaction table.
.I FORMAT
is
.BR csv ,
.B json
or
.BR svg .
.TP
.BI \-\-pocket " FILE"
Pocket definition for the fingerprint (residue, position label and region, one position per line).
Requires
.BR \-\-fingerprint .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the usage and the default thresholds.
.PP
All the geometric thresholds can be changed from the command line:
.BR \-\-hb\-min ,
.BR \-\-hb\-max ,
.BR \-\-hb\-ha ,
.BR \-\-hb\-angle ,
.BR \-\-hb\-long ,
.BR \-\-hb\-long\-tol ,
.BR \-\-hb\-ante ,
.BR \-\-hyd\-min ,
.BR \-\-hyd\-max ,
.BR \-\-salt\-max ,
.BR \-\-salt\-centroid ,
.BR \-\-rep\-max ,
.BR \-\-hal\-max ,
.BR \-\-hal\-angle ,
.BR \-\-metal\-max ,
.BR \-\-pi\-max ,
.BR \-\-pi\-offset ,
.BR \-\-pi\-angle ,
.BR \-\-cp\-max ,
.BR \-\-clash ,
.BR \-\-wb\-min ,
.BR \-\-wb\-max .
Run
.B ligint \-\-help
for the default values.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error: file that cannot be opened, unknown option, missing or non-numeric value, malformed residue number.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the ligands of a structure:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ligint 1AZM.pdb
.fi
.RE
.PP
Interactions of the ligand AZM, as CSV, with the PLIP-like preset:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ligint 1AZM.pdb AZM \-\-plip\-like \-\-csv > interactions.csv
.fi
.RE
.PP
Interaction fingerprint as a figure, using alternate conformation B and a pocket definition:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ligint 3EYG.pdb LIG A 1 \-\-altloc B \-\-fingerprint svg \-\-pocket pocket.tsv > figure.svg
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/ligint
Documentation, including the fingerprint format and an example pocket definition.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ligint\-gui (1)
.SH AUTHORS
The ligint authors.
